{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KDNcZqwcHcSntwBfzu7Bn5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies correctness through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with `cmd/` per-utility packages, shared `pkg/` libraries (testutils, sys, format), and `magefiles/` build infrastructure. Differential testing via `pkg/testutils` is the gating verification mechanism.\n\n**Implementation State** (based on source_code, which is authoritative):\n- **Code exists**: `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge` — all have implementation and library test files\n- **Tests missing**: `cmd/cat/cat_test.go` and `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` are absent from source_code — no differential tests for either utility\n- **No code**: `cmd/du`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/ts`, `cmd/ls`, trivial utilities (true/false/yes/basename/dirname), tee, head, seq\n\n**Current Release Priority**: rel00.0 (foundational) is effectively complete. **rel01.1 (cat)** is the earliest incomplete release — implementation exists but differential tests do not.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete work is **rel01.1-uc001-cat**: `cmd/cat/main.go` exists (282 lines, covers R1–R5) but `cmd/cat/cat_test.go` does not appear in source_code. Per P5 (test before downstream code) and P8 (implementation before tests within a feature), the cat differential test file is the highest-priority task. It must exist before rel01.2+ work can proceed, since cat validates the test harness integration pattern that all subsequent utilities will follow.\n\nScoping to 4 sub-requirements: R1.1 (file concatenation), R1.2 (stdin reading), R5.2 (error messages), R5.3 (exit codes) — these cover core I/O and error handling, the foundation all other cat tests depend on.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cat differential tests for prd006-cat R1.1, R1.2, R5.2, R5.3\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd006-cat.yaml (cat PRD -- R1 file reading, R5 error and exit code requirements)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.1.yaml (cat test suite specification with concrete test inputs)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (existing cat implementation -- understand catFile, reportError, exit code logic)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests API, NormalizeFunc, buildEnv)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go (reference for TestMain binary-building pattern and subprocess test structure)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/cat_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for cat core I/O and error handling (R1.1, R1.2, R5.2, R5.3)\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test that cat concatenates named files in argument order to stdout, verifying byte-for-byte output parity with GNU gcat reference binary (prd006-cat R1.1)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test that cat reads from stdin when no file arguments are given and when \\\"-\\\" appears as a file argument, verifying output matches gcat (prd006-cat R1.2)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test that cat writes per-file error messages to stderr for nonexistent files and continues processing remaining file arguments (prd006-cat R5.2)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test that cat exits with code 0 on success and code 1 when any file argument produces an error (prd006-cat R5.3)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.RunDiffTests with testutils.DiffTest cases per the pkg/testutils/difftest.go API. Each test case specifies Name, Args, Stdin, and ExitCode fields.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Reference binary is gcat (GNU cat installed via Homebrew). Locate via exec.LookPath(\\\"gcat\\\") in TestMain; skip all tests with t.Skip if gcat is not found.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Build the Go cat binary from cmd/cat/ using 'go build -o <tmpdir>/cat ./cmd/cat' in TestMain. Store paths in package-level vars for use by test functions. Follow the TestMain pattern in pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"All tests inherit LC_ALL=C from the testutils.RunDiffTests harness via buildEnv. Do not set LC_ALL manually in DiffTest.Env.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/cat/cat_test.go compiles without errors -- go vet ./cmd/cat/... passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All differential tests pass when gcat reference binary is available on PATH\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests include cases for single-file read, multi-file concatenation in argument order, stdin-only (no args), and \\\"-\\\" as a file argument interspersed with named files\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Tests verify stderr output and exit code 1 for nonexistent file arguments, including a case where valid and invalid files are mixed\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Test file follows project conventions -- copyright header, SPDX-License-Identifier MIT, package main, t.Parallel() on test functions that do not share mutable state\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54229,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54229},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eed5adc3-57e8-4541-bf11-7c2e7d55c52b","uuid":"96e4fc64-266e-4a0a-960c-9956b321b913"}
